    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1993, residents adopted a formal Woodlawn Neighborhood Plan to guide future growth and community development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://gowoodlawn.com/category/woodlawn-history/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Like many Northeast Portland neighborhoods, Woodlawn is experiencing gentrification, with 15 owner‑occupied homes and only five tenant‑occupied on the 12th Avenue block.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woodlawn%2C_Portland%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Woodlawn borders Sunderland to the north, Concordia to the east, King and Vernon to the south, and Piedmont to the west.",
